# Specs & fixtures

- Auth flows: `import { test, expect } from '../../fixtures/auth.fixture.js'` then `await loginAs(users.superAdmin)`.
- Users from `test-data/users.js` only — never hardcode passwords in specs.
- Arrange → Act → Assert; keep specs thin; put UI steps in page objects / `utils/e2eWorkflow.js`.
- Multi-step E2E: use `e2eState` persistence; serial mode + higher timeout when dependent.
- Prefer stable assertions (URL, role headings, API-backed checks via `utils/network.js`) over sleep.
- Do not add `test.only` / `test.skip` without reason; `forbidOnly` is on in CI.

```js
test('SA can open Clients', async ({ page, loginAs }) => {
  await loginAs(users.superAdmin);
  const clients = new ClientsPage(page);
  await clients.goto();
  await clients.expectLoaded();
});
```
